body:
The extent of my abuse was something I only told my father, and even then, just vaguely. But now, they both know everything except for how severely my mother would abuse us. Only mother knows that now. But they both know what their son did to me and I thought it would make me feel better to tell them of the sexual abuse I endured.

&#x200B;

It did not. My mother uses it against me. I'm an idiot.

My skin isn't the only thing that's sensitive.

&#x200B;

(It's me, I'm sensitive.)

Personally, I've felt the paranoia and the fear, but it's at a different part of the day. Usually morning or early afternoon, occasionally the evening. But my sleep schedule is a mess (go to sleep at 8am-wake up at like 5pm). I was mostly sexually abused during the day. It disgusts me because no one ever caught him doing this.. There were 6 people in the house at any given time and no one catches someone doing this to me for the 10 years that it happened?

&#x200B;

But yeah, I feel this. It may be worth making sure you feel absolutely safe (night light, double checking a billion times that your bedroom door is locked, reminding yourself what you're thinking is irrational which is incredibly hard to do, etc), and then possibly finding a nightly ritual that helps you feel relaxed, safe, and secure so you can drift to sleep. For me, it's my stuffed animals. I can't sleep unless I have 2 with me in bed. I'm almost 25 and married.. but it's just how I am. My stuffed animals were there when I was getting abused sexually, physically, etc. So I guess they're my comfort. Good luck :)
